  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the following circuit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math>. The charge stored in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;C</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0003_82e66b403781.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 140px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>From circuit given,</p><p>Capacitors&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are in parallel connection with constant potential difference as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p>Now, charge stored in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>"
